# Humber Hawk Mk VI four-door saloon, 1954-1959.
#
# The big Humber of the mid-1950s: 4,648 mm long, 1,778 mm wide, 1,626 mm high,
# 2,794 mm wheelbase; 2,267 cc four. The Mk VI introduced the enlarged boot and
# wraparound rear window; the VIa followed in 1957. Rootes' upper-middle saloon,
# used as a directors' car and by police forces.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humber_Hawk
#
# Colours: Black, Sage Green, Dove Grey and Maroon are documented Humber finishes
# of the period.
#
# Weight: 55 in total (black 20, grey 14, green 12, maroon 9), low per section F of
# the gaps doc.
#
# Speed 135 km/h; comfort 100/480 (line). Classes 2,3.
# Dates: 1954-1967, the tail covering later life on British roads.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/humber-hawk-vi.blend. References:
# citycars/references/humber-hawk-vi/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=HumberHawkVI(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=20
intro_year=1954
intro_month=7
retire_year=1967
retire_month=6
speed=135
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=100
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=480

